 "finished_by_agent": true,
 "finish_summary": "Starting from the flat 32-input adder-chain popcount (area 264.7 um2, WNS 7.016 ns, score 69.899), I first probed the flow's timing structure: a logic-free design reaches only WNS \u2248 7.86, revealing ~2.0 ns fixed input-delay overhead and a similar ~2.1 ns output-side overhead, so score is dominated by combinational depth (10 points per ns) rather than area (0.001 per um2). Since the checker proves sequential equivalence with a different state encoding (verified), I retimed the function across the register boundary: the pre-register stage computes four byte popcounts (carry-save full/half-adder network, with each byte's MSB simplified to an 8-input AND) plus one column-wise CSA level, storing 13 bits; the post-register stage finishes with a 4-bit carry-lookahead add, and the MSB of the result is taken directly from a precomputed all-ones flag, removing the top carry. The hold (\"update only when valid\") was moved from enable muxes in front of the pipeline registers to a single output mux with an unconditional-load register pair, which shortens the input path and lets the partial-result registers be reset-free DFFs. Measured probes showed the input path (2.426 ns) and output path (2.401 ns) are balanced within half a gate level, so further level-shifting was not profitable. Final verified result: simulate PASS, equivalence PROVEN, post-route area 361.5 um2, WNS 7.5268 ns, score 74.907 (+5.01 over baseline).",
